# .trivyignore — scoped, documented, time-boxed exceptions to the image
# HIGH/CRITICAL gate. NOTHING in this file applies to the app, worker or
# migrator images: the workflow wires it into ONLY the two fayanms-backup
# scan steps (tests/audit/r3-2026-1018-physical-basebackup-promotion.test.ts
# pins that wiring and asserts every entry is documented).
#
# 2026-10-18 — the `age` encryption binary (Go) inside fayanms-backup
# carries the Go-stdlib advisories below. Trivy attributes them to the age
# apk package; the fixes land in GO releases (1.25.10+/1.26.3+ per the
# advisory ranges), so they clear only when Alpine rebuilds/reships the age
# package against a patched Go toolchain — no fixed build was available at
# this date. The `age` binary handles ONLY ciphertext on the wire/pipe and
# the recipient public key; none of these DoS/parsing vectors is reachable
# through attacker-controlled backup INPUT in our pipeline (pg_dump /
# pg_basebackup output → age stdin), and the sidecar runs non-root,
# cap-drop-ALL, read-only rootfs.
# OWNER FOLLOW-UP (tracked in GA-READINESS row 3 + STATE.md): when Alpine
# ships a rebuilt age (or a newer upstream release), remove these entries
# and re-run the gate. Review by: 2026-11-18 (30 days).
